  "content_en": "The Biography of Empress Xiaohui Zhang of Han Dynasty (with postscript) This should be the biography of Empress Xiaohui Zhang mentioned in the book review. It's indeed gorgeous, I love it too. It is said to have been commissioned by people of the Eastern Jin Dynasty. I tried reading the \"Book of Han·The Biography of Empress Xiaohui Zhang\" in the past, and I suspected that the narrative was a little short. Everything recorded in the biography is all about Empress Dowager Lu. I also read the \"Five Elements Chronicles\", which records the disaster of the weaving room in the fourth year of Emperor Hui's reign. He thought it was a sign of Empress Zhang's loss of virtue and a sign of desolation. Disasters in the husband's palace are a common occurrence, but it is unreasonable to attribute the blame to the newly established Zhang Hou. Later, he entered the palace as a child, but he was widowed at an early age. He was not interested in foreign affairs, and even the affairs in the palace were in charge of the Empress Dowager Lu. It was in vain for the ministers to move the angry Empress Zhang and set up a secluded Beigong because of the Lu family. It would be in vain for historians to take advantage of the hidden world and blame it for their lack of morality. It was Min Ranzhi who used it, and then he studied the chronicles and biographies of \"History\" and \"Han\", studied all the histories, searched for barnyard records, and also read novels. He picked up more than fifty kinds of them and wrote a piece of \"Wai Zhuan\". For more than ten years, I have not dared to come out. When I heard about Yongjia, some of the Han Mausoleums were stolen, and some of them were noted by Gao Hui, Wen Jing and the Four Dynasties of the Han Dynasty, and spread to Jiangzuo. After an urgent visit, I obtained three volumes of \"Xiang Nu Jing\", two volumes of \"Records of Concubines of Xianghan Palace\", and \"Genealogy of the Zhang Family in Guanzhong\". They were read together and occasionally used to supplement the previous biography. The peerless virtue of Zhang Empress was related to the reason why she was falsely accused of seclusion at that time. Empress Xiaohui of the Han Dynasty, her surname was Yan, her courtesy name was Meng Yu, and her nickname was Shujun. Huidi's sister is the eldest daughter of Princess Lu Yuan. When the first emperor was the pavilion chief, he married Empress Lu and gave birth to a daughter and a son. The male is Emperor Xiaohui, and the female is Princess Lu Yuan. In the second year of Emperor Gaodi's reign, the Han army was defeated at Pengcheng, and Empress Lu was captured by Chu. Emperor Gao met Emperor Hui and his princess on the road and carried them on their way, but their horses were tired and they were captured behind. The emperor crumpled his two sons and wanted to abandon them, but Teng Gong often came down to collect them and carried them slowly. Facing Yongshu Naichi, the soldier was able to escape between Xiayi, and then brought him into the pass. At that time, Emperor Hui was six years old and the princess was twelve years old. In the sixth month of the Han Dynasty, the capital of the Han Dynasty was Yueyang. The crown prince was established and the sons of the princes were appointed as guards. The princess was very virtuous and kind, and Emperor Gao loved her very much. The emperor said: \"We should choose a good son-in-law for him.\" Zhang Er's son Ao Fang stayed in the Han Dynasty in Wei. He was fourteen years old and had a very handsome appearance. Xu Negative Prime Minister said: I should be a king and a marquis, and give birth to a daughter with excellent virtues and beauty. Ao Wei's letter. The emperor's beloved Ao Dujin was named Princess. In the fourth month of summer in the fifth year, Princess Aoshang became the king of Zhao, and in the seventh month of autumn, she moved to Zhao, and the princess became the queen. On the third day of the third month of the sixth year, a daughter was born in Handan. Five-colored clouds covered the palace, and the sound of fairy music could be faintly heard in the air. Ao was born charming, so she named her Yan. When he was several years old, he became gentle and quiet. He had no teeth and could not leave the pavilion. Zhang Ao said to the princess: \"A Yan is kind to others and behaves dignifiedly. Her future blessings are immeasurable, but she is afraid that if she is too kind and kind, she will be deceived by others.\" In the ninth year, Zhang Ao was deposed as Marquis Xuanping, and his family members all moved to Chang'an. Emperor Huigao used Lou Jingce to marry Princess Lu Yuan to the Huns. The princess cried to Zhang Ao day and night, and A Yan also held the princess's clothes and cried. Emperor Gao took pity on him when he heard about it, and Empress Lu tried her best to speak to the emperor, but she stopped. When A Yan was five or six years old, her appearance was extremely beautiful. Whenever his mother came in and out of the palace, Emperor Gao often ordered Mrs. Qi to hold her in her arms, feed her with fruit bait, and say to her: \"Although you are unparalleled in beauty, this girl will be beyond your reach in ten years.\" When Emperor Hui was the crown prince, he married a certain daughter of a meritorious official as his concubine. The concubine also often hugged Ayan for joy. When Emperor Hui came to the throne, he did not have three years of mourning and could not establish a queen. When the concubine passed away, the emperor was moved by the change of the pig. He specializes in hiding his secrets and entertains himself with wine and sex. There are many beauties in the harem, and they dote on beautiful boys and children, lying down and getting up with them. During the reign of Emperor Hui, all the ministers and ministers were painted with powder and wore crowns with turtlenecks, which was the custom of Hong children. After the establishment of the emperor, he wanted to visit the daughter of a famous nobleman with outstanding grace and virtue. The Queen Mother often felt pity for Ao's degeneration and wanted to marry Ao's daughter to the emperor. She said to the emperor: \"A Yan is the nephew of the emperor's family and the daughter of the royal family. She has no equal in the world, and her beauty is unparalleled in ancient and modern times. I choose it.\" The emperor said: \"What is the order of good ethics? She is still young.\" The queen mother said: \"You are too young to grow up, and your nephew is not among the five ethics. Why don't you hear that Duke Wen of Jin wants to marry Wen Ying?\" The emperor obeyed the order and ordered the ministers to discuss the ceremony. In the spring of the third year, the Empress Dowager sent Changle Shaofu and Zongzheng to accept the emperor's proposal, with a bundle of silk and wild goose biscuits, four horses, and to ask for an audience with his daughter. Eight people from Fu Mu supported the girl, and she stood facing the south in full attire. She is only ten years old, and the Queen Mother is afraid that people will judge her young age. The messenger claimed to be twelve years old, and when he asked for his name, he told the temple that all the rituals were the same. However, Yan's physique is already as good as that of Twelve or Thirteen. Everyone who saw it stared at him and licked his tongue, thinking that he was a fairy. He also played a memorial, saying that the daughter of Marquis Ping has a pure appearance, is well-trained in etiquette, and has a mother.The virtue of etiquette and graceful appearance should be inherited from Tianzuo and worshiped in the ancestral temple. The prime minister, Taiwei Bo, the imperial censor Yao, and the Taishi used Tailuo to report to the temple, and used rituals to divine the auspicious month and day. The questions about the name, the acceptance of auspiciousness, the acceptance of the levy, the date of request, and the grand ceremony were all determined by Taifu Shusun Tong. The betrothal ceremony included twelve horses and twenty thousand catties of gold, which was unprecedented since ancient times. Since the emperor of the Han Dynasty established the latter, it must be based on the story of Emperor Xiaohui's acceptance of the queen. The younger brother Yan, who was still young, saw a lot of gold lying in the hall. He rushed in and said, \"Sister Yan, the emperor has bought you.\" Princess Lu Yuan scolded her and said, \"Don't say much, little kid.\" Yan Nai took her sister's hand and said, \"Sister, why don't you go out to see?\" The Han Dynasty followed the Qin system, and every time a concubine was admitted, a female official who knew how to look after her would be sent to examine her. In autumn and August, the imperial edict (this bird) was issued to the marquis Xu Fu to the Xuanping Marquis. The one who promised to be negative was an old woman from Hanoi, and he was the one who granted the title of marquis because of his kindness. He led Nu Yan to the secret room and bathed her. Looking closely at Yan's face, she is long and slightly round, white and flawless, her cheeks are plump and shaped like a full moon, her eyebrows are like phoenix eyes, her temples are like dragons, her ears are big and drooping on her shoulders, and she is as white as her face. The chin is broad and round, and the light can tell people, the chest is flat, the shoulders are round and straight, the back is slightly thick, the waist is slender, the texture is greasy and clean, fat and infertile, and there are no hemorrhoids or ulcers, no sunspots, and other private diseases of the mouth, nose, armpits, and feet. Xu Negi wrote a book one by one, urging Yan to pay tribute to the emperor for ten thousand years. Yan was embarrassed and refused, so he persuaded him for the fourth time. Then he bowed slowly and whispered that he would be the emperor for ten thousand years. The negative form was secretly presented to the Queen Mother and Emperor Hui. The emperor was overjoyed after seeing it and paid it to the palace historian. In the tenth month of winter at Renyin, the imperial edict was sent to Prime Minister Xiangcan and the imperial censor Yao to welcome the queen Xuanping Houdi. The queen's dress is denuded at the top, with a deep collar and wide sleeves, and a gauze belt. The dress is so long that it touches the floor, with no feet visible. Wearing a dragon and phoenix bead crown on his head, waving gold and hairpins every step of the way, he bowed to the Zhang family's temple. When applying make-up, you should use fake hair as a rule. From now on, Fu Mu will have long hair like clouds and please leave with Princess Lu Yuan. Zhang Ao carried his daughter into the car, called the police, and entered the front hall of Weiyang Palace. The emperor comes to the throne, accompanied by hundreds of officials. To the north of the queen, the etiquette officer finished reading the book. Queen Liusu knelt down and bowed three times, and the female officials led her to the emperor to express her gratitude. Then he bowed down and there was no sound for a long time. The female official taught it by ear, and was later called \"Concubine Zhang Yan, congratulations to the Emperor for ten thousand years.\" Its subtle charm is like the breeze blowing the flute, and like the first call of an oriole. The emperor was moved and stood up. Taiwei Bo was awarded the seal and ribbon, and the regular servants knelt down to receive it, and he was conferred the title of female official. The female officer led the queen, who bowed down and called her concubine again. After thanking her for her kindness, she ascended the throne. All the officials took their seats and bowed before retreating. The empress entered the middle palace in a soft carriage, and the officials established themselves as emperors. Instead of marrying into the family of a meritorious official, they were selfish about their nephews. All of them had a sense of injustice. After arriving at the middle palace, the walls are all painted with gold, pepper is fragrant, embellished with pearls for curtains, carved sapphire for tables, sandalwood for the bed, inlaid with corals, red rhinestones for the tents, decorated with emeralds, brocade quilts and embroidered pillows, all with woven gold dragons and phoenixes. The other displays are filled with treasures and play, which are so bright that they cannot be described. The emperor and his queen performed the ceremony of union. Later, she followed the teachings of a female official and worshiped the emperor, claiming to be her niece Ayan and congratulating his majesty the uncle for ten thousand years. The emperor smiled and said: \"You still call me \"ye\" from the front.\" He also drank the wine from the gold bottle. Later, he was stunned and couldn't drink, so he barely finished a bottle. In the evening, I sat on the bed. The emperor held the candle and looked carefully, and saw the two servant girls with their heads hanging down behind them. They were pure and radiant, without any makeup, and the color was like the morning glow reflecting the snow, or like the pear blossom with the rain, and the positions of the various bodies were extremely wonderful. After that, he bowed his head in shame, mouthing on both sides, slightly dizzy like finger marks, like the waves of the waves. The emperor said to the queen: \"I always avoided suspicion because of your nephew, and I didn't look closely. Unexpectedly, your heart is so pleasant that it is so extreme.\" At that time, the queen was ten years old. Although he was in the middle palace, the emperor did not stay overnight. The affairs of the palace are left to the beauties and elders of the harem to take charge of. Seeing that the queen had no power, the harem tried to invade and insult her, and privately discussed: \"Although Zhang Shujun occupies an honorable position, she is really a virgin. And after entering the palace, how can I be afraid of us.\" Five days later, the queen mother presented the meal to the table, bowed and held her breath, feeling happy and solemn. After the emperor went to the Changle Palace in the East, every time he passed through the streets, he would visit many people and build a new road to belong to the Changle Palace. Every time after going out, the maid first moves the chariot into the inner room, then sits in it, puts on the curtains, and then walks around. Although people from the eunuch palace may not be able to see the back. After that, every morning when I was doing my makeup in the mirror, there was a little bird with colorful ornaments flying outside the curtain and singing, \"Shujun is wrapped up in her secluded room\", \"Shujun is wrapped up in her secluded room\", and it stayed like this for more than ten years. Later, after migrating to the North Palace, the birds never came again. In the spring and March of the fourth year, Emperor Hui was twenty. On the eleventh day of the following year, the emperor performed a crowning ceremony and led the queen to the Gaomiao. The peacocks and white cranes in the palace will dance when they see you. After Princess Lu Yuan came to the palace for a visit, she was given a welcome gift like a family member, expressing her attachment to her mother. The princess pointed to Emperor Hui and said, \"Are you satisfied with your wishes?\" The emperor said, \"Ayan is not like my eldest sister, but she is like Marquis Xuanping, which makes my sixth palace pink and white less beautiful.\"color. Her nature of calmness, wisdom and willingness is the same as that of her eldest sister. At that time, his younger brother Zhang Yan was at his side. The emperor held him in his arms and said, \"This son's physique is quite similar to that of his sister. If he were a woman, he would be a beautiful person.\" \"Every morning when the emperor gets up, he goes to the Jiao Room to watch the queen take a nap. He tastes the words of the palace people and says: \"The queen's beauty is so beautiful that she wants to compete with the white jade dish. \"Also said: \"The queen's expression is just like that of Xuan Pinghou, but her appearance is smaller than her ears. \"He was called \"Mr. Zhang\" because of the play. When Fu Mu saw the emperor approaching, he would first hold a gold spit bowl, fill it with crape myrtle and put it in, and then rinse his mouth with sandalwood. The emperor often held him behind him and put it on his knees, counting forty white teeth, and grinding them into pieces. The color of the back lips is like cherry blossoms, with a touch of red. One day, the emperor came to the harem and took off his clothes. The two palace people were washing the feet of the queen. The emperor sat and looked at her and said with a smile: \"Ayan is young but her feet are almost as long as mine.\" He also said to the palace people: \"The queen's shins are round, white and delicate. Who among your generation can match her?\" \"... In the first month of the spring of the seventh year, Emperor Hui hunted in Shangyuan. The queen and all the beauties rode behind him. They were all dressed like men. Their robes were either crimson, yellow or green. The back was made of fox white fur, the clothes were dark green, and the clothes were pure yellow. He wore a red brocade robe, and wiped his forehead with red gauze. He galloped and crossed, and the flowers and grass glowed, and they were all as graceful as twenty-eight beauties. I didn't know she was a concubine. Then I was so surprised that I undressed and went to the toilet. A wild pig rushed into the prisoner's back and broke his lower clothes. There was a slight injury on the back. The emperor was frightened and stabbed the pig with his sword. All the beauties congratulated him. The emperor smiled and said: \"How fat and white are you!\" \"The rear was shocked, ashamed and at a loss. He hurriedly called the maid to get in, his cheeks were dizzy, and he was silent for half a day. In April of summer, the queen kissed the silkworms, and came out in royal attire, riding on a Luan chariot, driving a four-horse horse, Zhang Qingyu, and nine dragon flags. The wife of the Taiwei rode in the imperial palace, and the wife of the Taiwei came to the imperial court. Chang'an ordered At the invitation, there were gold and yellow axes, and the guide was led by tigers and feathers. The queen bowed to collect mulberry in the silkworm palace, and carried three pots in the cocoon pavilion. After the ceremony, there were many people watching in Chang'an. \"At the beginning, when Marquis Piyang tried to eat, he was lucky enough to be rewarded by the Queen Mother. When Emperor Hui heard about it, he was angry at Marquis Biyang and sent him to prison. He was about to kill him and then released him. The Empress Dowager was ashamed and thought that the emperor had no children, and the beauty in the harem had many children, so it became even more difficult for him to do so. Yi, he wanted to denounce all the beauties in order to get the queen to be favored by Zhuan Fang. The emperor was very worried and had no idea, so he begged the queen to sleep with him. In order to weep and say that all the beauties are innocent, Concubine Yan thinks that she cannot have children, so the Queen Mother stops her. In May, the Queen Mother heard that the beauty in the harem was pregnant, and she became angry and wanted to kill her. Suddenly, the Queen Mother made a plan to kill her. Pretending to be pregnant for several months, she was about to give birth to a boy, who was named the Queen's son and was established as the Crown Prince. Later, he had no choice but to follow his advice and said to his mother, Princess Lu Yuan: \"Yan Yu has always been deeply ashamed of her petty behavior. However, if Yan has no children, the Queen Mother will eventually be unhappy, and the princes will also be in danger. The emperor's depression will increase and his illness will increase, so Yan is the one who entertains the queen mother, protects the prince, and harmonizes the two palaces, so as to calm the emperor's ears. \"The Empress Dowager issued an edict that the Empress would be pregnant until the end of the month, so she would not have to look at the moon. The Emperor also did not come to the harem for months, and the Empress lived in peace and quiet, never leaving the bedroom. The maids were cunning and whispered to each other: \"The Empress is going to give birth to a prince, but why is her belly not big? \"The beauty gave birth to a boy in June, and the Queen Mother sent him to take him, wrap him in a blanket, and send him to the harem to kill his mother. That day, the Queen Mother sent the concubine to the queen to pretend to have abdominal pain, but within a few seconds, the baby was already in her arms. He offered sacrifices to the ancestral temple and established him as the prince, and all the ministers paid tribute to him. Expressing congratulations. Three days later, the empress gave the beauty some medicine, Wenqi, and a hundred catties of gold. She was so frightened that the empress dowager handed her over, her red sleeves wet with tears, and she secretly told Emperor Hui, \"The reason why I tolerate this is because I want to save this person.\" If you still see people being killed today, isn't it because of bad luck? \"At that time, there were six sons in Emperor Hui's harem, and the one born after him was named the youngest. The queen cared for them all as if they were their own children, and took care of their mother. At this year, the emperor's younger brother Huainan Wang came to the dynasty, and the king's mother was the beauty of the Zhang Ao family. Ao Xian gave birth to the king after Gao Di, so he was married to the Zhang family. The most friendly. Then I asked Emperor Hui to go to the Queen. The emperor said: \"Your sister-in-law is not old enough, she is naive and fearful of people, and she is like a virgin.\" The king knelt down and bowed respectfully, and then bowed in the curtain, and said solemnly: \"Uncle Jiu is fine.\" Then he sat upright without saying a word or even looking up. The king retreated and said to others: \"My sister-in-law is the most beautiful person in ancient and modern times, and she is also the most kind person.\" \"In August, the emperor did not hesitate, and the queen asked about her illness. The emperor suddenly sent the queen to get on the bed, touched her breasts and sighed: \"Ayan has grown up now, and I can't bear to let go of her. However, your body is so thick that you may become thinner for me in the future. There is such a personBut if you can't live happily as a couple for a day, you are also a husband. \"Wu Yin, the emperor died in Weiyang Palace at the age of twenty-three. He was fourteen years later. He cried like a ritual, bathed like a ritual, and then gathered. The princes, kings and ministers stood in front of their highness, the queen was in the palace, facing east, and the prince was facing west, all crying. All the concubines, princesses, and wives all came to the palace from the queen, no less than a hundred. Princess Lu Yuan was also there. The ministers heard her voice from afar, and were crying. Looking at her from a distance, she was the youngest, and her face was as beautiful as a peach. When the crown prince ascended the throne, the queen mother lived in the main hall of the Weiyang Palace. She was later called Queen Xiaohui and still lived in the Jiao Room of the middle palace. The queen mother wanted to take advantage of this time to punish the meritorious officials, but the queen mother kept her words secret, and outsiders did not know what to do at that time. Entering the Queen Mother's bed, Zhang Qing saw that the Queen Mother was walking around like a virgin. She didn't dare to sit down without asking, and she spoke to Zhao Yin, thinking that she didn't see anything in the picture, and said: \"I want to know Queen Zhang, but I have seen her younger brother Zhang Yan, and I know that she is already ten to five or six.\" \"On the fifteenth day of the following year, Princess Lu Yuan passed away, and the Queen Mother sent the Queen home to attend her mother's death. Since she was young and weak, she was living alone, feeling sad and sad, so she composed a song and said in her words: \"As a child, I entered the Jiao Fang and waited silently for the late Emperor. If your fate is not good, your late emperor will pass away. After holding Pu, you will guard the empty bed. Enjoy the beautiful night with bright candles, and admire the flying stars in the sky. Complaining about wealth and ridicule for entertainment is not as good as the chaff of a gangster. When does the long night come, the bright moon shines with weak shadows? We are chatting and thinking about the past, as if my uncle was by the side; when the wind blows back, I wake up in surprise, and my mind suddenly seems to be dead. I wipe my tears from my tent, and I am hesitant when I walk on my feet. The chickens sing in chorus to announce the dawn, thinking of my uncle and splitting his liver and intestines; hoping for the same hole after death, and worshiping the clear light underground. \"So the Queen Mother ordered Piyanghou to supervise the Weiyang Palace as the right prime minister and live in the palace to serve the Queen Mother. All matters in the palace belong to Yan. Piyanghou pursued and blamed Emperor Hui, and gave Queen Xiaohui some daily food and drink, cutting it down by more than half. Later, Shao Ai wanted to poison Emperor Hui, so he bribed the queen's maid and asked about Queen Yan's personal affairs. One of the maids tasted the words and said: \"I have served the Queen for the longest time, and I know it in detail. The Queen does not lean lazily when she is standing, does not have a lazy look when she sits, has a regular routine in her daily life, has a regular place in her movements, and eats and drinks that are above those of a normal person. The server is good to play, and it is different from the current customs. When you cough and spit on the ground, there will be mushrooms every time. Their fragrance is not as strong as the fragrance of orchids. Although there is no slight sweat in the hot summer, there is no slight odor in the feces, and there is no snoring in sleep, we are treated neatly and kindly, and we do not add any harsh words to each other. ...The postscript says: If there are two chapters in the biography of Empress Xiaohui, this is the first chapter. I did not pass on the author's surname, but I found out that it was written by a person from the Eastern Jin Dynasty. I searched extensively and gathered information to help correct the case for Ban Shi, and to rectify A Yan's injustice. When combined with the later chapters, they are probably written by one person and can be read together.",
  "translated": true
